# LOCK-ON FROM ABOVE (owner, 2026-09-24: "it needs to lock the player's movement
# so they are facing the target they are locked onto"; docs/CONTROLS.md
# §Lock-on). Through the real keys: Z locks a machine and the body turns onto it;
# a strafe bends round it and the body keeps facing it; a dodge goes where the
# keys point and still faces it; a swing goes at it; the lock cycled to another
# machine turns the body onto that one; the view over the shoulder is taken and
# left again with the lock still held; the machine is broken and the lock is
# handed on; letting go turns the body back onto its walk.
# From above the keys stay the screen's; a held key sideways arcs round the lock
# at the distance it started instead of leaving on a tangent.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/lockon_top.tour --seed=4 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --give=axe_felling:1 --held=axe_felling
coast calm
wait 0.8
spawn runner
wait 0.8
shot 01-a-machine-before-the-lock with mob:runner

hold target
await target 5
await lock_facing 3
wait 0.4
shot 02-locked-and-facing-it with target:runner,lock_facing

walk 1,0 1.4
await lock_circled 2
shot 03-strafed-round-it-still-facing with mob:runner,lock_facing

tap dodge
wait 0.25
shot 04-dodged-still-facing with mob:runner,lock_facing

# A blow may ring off plate or meet a machine that turned: a player who misses
# goes round and tries again (lockon_shoulder does the same).
try 8
await target:runner 0.3
walkto part 3
press swing
await hit 1.2
end
wait 0.2
shot 05-swung-at-the-lock with mob:runner,lock_facing

spawn cutter
wait 0.6
tap target_next
await target 3
wait 0.5
await lock_facing 3
shot 06-cycled-and-turned-onto-the-next with mob:cutter,target:cutter,lock_facing

tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
await shoulder_locked 3
wait 0.4
shot 07-over-the-shoulder-the-lock-kept with target:cutter,shoulder_locked,lock_facing

tap shoulder
await top_view 3
await target 1
wait 0.4
shot 08-back-above-the-lock-kept with target:cutter,lock_facing

release target
await target_none 5
walk 0,1 0.8
shot 09-let-go-and-walking-on
